WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:02.120
You're at home watching a movie.

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:05.680
Maybe it's a great film, or maybe it's just
a guilty pleasure, but you know for sure there's

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:08.059
that one scene you just don't want to watch.

00:00:08.059 --> 00:00:13.570
It's too cringe-worthy, too scary, too disturbing,
too stupid — or even too boring — so you

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:16.820
grab the remote so you can fast forward to
the next watchable scene.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:18.390
Don't worry, everyone's done it.

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:22.090
Here are some of the movie moments that many
of us prefer to skip right over.

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:24.010
Spoilers ahead, of course.

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:25.010
Jaws

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:29.289
This Steven Spielberg classic still gives
everyone shark nightmares, and it all stems

00:00:29.289 --> 00:00:30.720
from its opening scene.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:35.079
The poor doomed Chrissie goes for a moonlight
skinny dip after a party on the beach.

00:00:35.079 --> 00:00:38.649
We see something approach her dangling legs
from under the water — and you can probably

00:00:38.649 --> 00:00:40.040
guess where it goes from there.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:44.229
With terror in her eyes, she's whipped around
for what seems like forever, screaming things

00:00:44.229 --> 00:00:45.229
like...

00:00:45.229 --> 00:00:47.539
"Oh it hurts!"

00:00:47.539 --> 00:00:50.469
...until she's finally pulled under for good.

00:00:50.469 --> 00:00:54.959
Better to just move along because we all know
the real fun of Jaws is watching Brody, Hooper,

00:00:54.959 --> 00:00:58.120
and Quint on the boat, hashing it out with
the shark.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:00:59.209
Scarface

00:00:59.209 --> 00:01:03.989
The rags-to-riches story of a Cuban immigrant
who becomes a drug lord only to see his empire

00:01:03.989 --> 00:01:06.740
crumble at his bloodied, cocaine-caked feet.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:11.940
It's a given that Scarface is a very violent
experience — but one scene featuring a chainsaw

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.500
takes it to another level.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:18.970
Early in the game, some seriously angry Colombians
show Tony Montana why you don't mess with

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:19.970
them by taking a chainsaw to one of his friends
while he has to watch.

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:23.000
Sure, there are plenty of horror movies that
use this particular tool to gruesome effect

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.070
— and you may choose to skip over those
scenes as well — but when it comes to the

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:30.000
Scarface chainsaw scene, you'll definitely
want to sit this one out.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.000
Misery

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:35.490
You don't really see it coming, but when whackadoo
Annie decides she needs to teach her "favorite"

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:39.500
author Paul a lesson after he breaks her rules,
it's pretty horrifying.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:43.561
With Paul tied to a bed with a wooden block
between his feet, Annie starts talking about

00:01:43.561 --> 00:01:47.340
how he needs a good "hobbling" to make him
realize he can never leave her — and then

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:51.090
she takes a sledgehammer and crushes his ankles
on both sides.

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:52.880
It's just too painful to watch.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.600
"Almost done."

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:59.320
By the way, in Stephen King's novel, Annie
does far worse things to poor Paul, but you

00:01:59.321 --> 00:02:01.770
can skip past those pages as well.

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:03.000
Marathon Man

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:06.810
Anyone who's seen Marathon Man probably gets
a toothache just thinking about it.

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:11.750
This superb crime thriller film sees graduate
student Babe caught up in a spy game that

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:16.330
involves a Nazi war criminal — a skilled
dentist whose specialty in the concentration

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:18.780
camps was, well, you get the picture.

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:21.240
He captures Babe and tortures him, all while
asking...

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:24.500
"Is it safe?"

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:30.040
No, it's not safe, and anyone with a dentist
phobia — which is pretty much everyone — will

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:32.300
probably push that fast-forward button.

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:33.940
127 Hours

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:37.760
If you know the true story of Aron Ralston,
a mountain climber who became trapped under

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:41.750
a boulder while hiking alone, you know the
desperate measures he had to take in order

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:42.750
to survive.

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:47.029
Played by James Franco in the film, Aron has
to saw off part of his arm in order to free

00:02:47.029 --> 00:02:48.689
himself and stay alive.

00:02:48.689 --> 00:02:53.150
When it comes to that moment in 127 Hours,
you think you're prepared, but you're really

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:54.150
not.

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:57.450
Director Danny Boyle masterfully captures
the essence of the scene, Franco brilliantly

00:02:57.450 --> 00:02:59.310
plays it, and they should be applauded for
it.

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:01.299
But no one needs to watch it again.

00:03:01.299 --> 00:03:02.950
2001: A Space Odyssey

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:08.139
Look, we all know this 1968 Stanley Kubrick
film was way ahead of its time when it was

00:03:08.139 --> 00:03:12.379
released, and is widely regarded as a cinematic
classic from a master director.

00:03:12.379 --> 00:03:15.579
It is a spectacularly visual film worthy of
its praise.

00:03:15.579 --> 00:03:19.439
But man, that first ten minutes, with the
apes and the black monolith, will put you

00:03:19.439 --> 00:03:20.459
right to sleep.

00:03:20.459 --> 00:03:22.010
"I don't know what you're talking about."

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:25.810
Just skip all that and get to the meat of
the film, in which a ship computer goes creepily

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:28.980
rogue after it realizes the humans might turn
it off.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:33.269
In the battle of evil computers versus dumb
monkeys, computers always win.

00:03:33.269 --> 00:03:34.510
Thanks for watching!

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:36.939
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:03:36.939 --> 00:03:39.000
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

